    description: "Tcl: tree-sitter-tcl parses braced literal arguments of ordinary commands as scripts, so regsub -all {::} $x {__} w still emits a call edge to an unresolved '__' (PR 3 removed the '::' form only).\n\nRepro: a .tcl file with that line -> a calls edge to a '__' stand-in.\n\nCLOSE WHEN braced arguments of commands that take no script (regsub, string map, ...) make no call edge.\n\nFound by the PR 3 (stable-id v16) WI-rozod/WI-zolat build, 2026-11-19; evidence ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/rozod/RESULTS.md (Residuals)."  # 5b19
